        {
          "id": 1,
          "title": "Lot 47 is on the drum",
          "content": "This week we are running Lot 47, a washed Guji we cupped last Thursday and could not put down. Blueberry up front, jasmine on the finish. On the shelf until it sells out.",
          "image_url": null,
          "category": "This week",
          "published": 1,
          "created_at": "2026-07-07T20:50:05.387Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-07-07T20:50:05.387Z"
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "title": "Why we drop the Alleyway at 198C",
          "content": "A few degrees past first crack is where this Guji shows its florals without turning grassy. Any hotter and the jasmine folds into toast. It is a narrow window, and we chase it every batch.",
          "image_url": null,
          "category": "Roasting notes",
          "published": 1,
          "created_at": "2026-07-07T20:50:05.395Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-07-07T20:50:05.395Z"
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "title": "Cupping the new Guatemala",
          "content": "Six lots on the table this morning, one clear winner: an Antigua with dried fig and brown butter. It becomes this month Ember Seasonal starting Friday.",
          "image_url": null,
          "category": "Cupping",
          "published": 1,
          "created_at": "2026-07-07T20:50:05.403Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-07-07T20:50:05.403Z"
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "title": "Delivering by bike all summer",
          "content": "Every wholesale order inside the neighbourhood goes out by cargo bike, roasted the morning it ships. No idling vans, no day-old beans.",
          "image_url": null,
          "category": "News",
          "published": 1,
          "created_at": "2026-07-07T20:50:05.411Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-07-07T20:50:05.411Z"
        }
      ]
    },
